(3728886, 515992, 39531, '<td valign="top">nice composition and use of color</td>', 'nice composition and use of color', '2007-06-02 13:55:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(3729386, 514120, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Oh, what a lovely image!  Yet you scored so very low.<br/> <br/>This is the most clear-cut example of a subtle photograph our hasty voters found DNMC that I''ve seen yet.  Of course it met the Challenge, but our hasty voters didn''t take the time to find the blue eyes of the model.  <br/> <br/>You did a beautiful job of photographing this model and you can certainly feel good about that.  You just didn''t hit our voters between the eyes. (ooops, sorry about the pun) <br/> <br/>I can only say "better luck next time" and keep up the very good work.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Oh, what a lovely image!  Yet you scored so very low. This is the most clear-cut example of a subtle photograph our hasty voters found DNMC that I''ve seen yet.  Of course it met the Challenge, but our hasty voters didn''t take the time to find the blue eyes of the model.   You did a beautiful job of photographing this model and you can certainly feel good about that.  You just didn''t hit our voters between the eyes. (ooops, sorry about the pun)  I can only say "better luck next time" and keep up the very good work.', '2007-06-02 16:29:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(3729397, 516890, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>I looked with care at your image and while I was marshalling my thoughts, I decided to look at the comments you received on this photograph.  Well, you were lucky enough to get a critique from <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=5792" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">StDavidson</a> and he said all the things I was going to say and then some!<br/> <br/>So my critique is: do what <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=5792" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">StDavidson</a> says to do, and by all means, continue to enjoy your DPC experience.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  I looked with care at your image and while I was marshalling my thoughts, I decided to look at the comments you received on this photograph.  Well, you were lucky enough to get a critique from  StDavidson and he said all the things I was going to say and then some! So my critique is: do what  StDavidson says to do, and by all means, continue to enjoy your DPC experience.', '2007-06-02 16:36:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(3729406, 515205, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>These pencil shots are always interesting because they can be done so many different ways.  <br/> <br/>You selected a symetrical composition, and it almost works.  I think  if the bottom three pencils were in exact alignment with the upper group it would have helped and also, if all the tips were sharpened to the same degree.   The camera records every little detail, so all these little things count!  Finally, I think it would have also been nice if the bottom three leads were in color, as well.  But all that said, you have a very nice clean image here and it presents well.<br/> <br/>It looks as if you are enjoying your experience at DPC and I''ll look forward to seeing more of your work.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  These pencil shots are always interesting because they can be done so many different ways.   You selected a symetrical composition, and it almost works.  I think  if the bottom three pencils were in exact alignment with the upper group it would have helped and also, if all the tips were sharpened to the same degree.   The camera records every little detail, so all these little things count!  Finally, I think it would have also been nice if the bottom three leads were in color, as well.  But all that said, you have a very nice clean image here and it presents well. It looks as if you are enjoying your experience at DPC and I''ll look forward to seeing more of your work. ', '2007-06-02 16:44:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(3729440, 516153, 12253, '<td valign="top">Quite a bit underrated.  Very nice!</td>', 'Quite a bit underrated.  Very nice!', '2007-06-02 17:00:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3729587, 516355, 56658, '<td valign="top">greetings from the critique club.<br/> <br/>Well, what is there to say about a 6.5 13th place shot:)<br/> <br/>On the positive side, I would say that it was a very good idea and very bold considering DPC generally dislikes nudes. I mean 9 votes of 3 and under is too many but not bad for a nude. I like the composition allot.<br/> <br/>The only thing that prevented me from voting higher was the look on her skin and the shoe. I see now that the shadows/highlights is the reason for the look. Without seeing the original I have no way of knowing if it was necessary.<br/> <br/>Either way it is a great shot. congrats on the nice finish.</td>', 'greetings from the critique club. Well, what is there to say about a 6.5 13th place shot:) On the positive side, I would say that it was a very good idea and very bold considering DPC generally dislikes nudes. I mean 9 votes of 3 and under is too many but not bad for a nude. I like the composition allot. The only thing that prevented me from voting higher was the look on her skin and the shoe. I see now that the shadows/highlights is the reason for the look. Without seeing the original I have no way of knowing if it was necessary. Either way it is a great shot. congrats on the nice finish.', '2007-06-02 17:43:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3729732, 516685, 4162, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on a new personal best-I love this picture!!</td>', 'Congratulations on a new personal best-I love this picture!!', '2007-06-02 18:35:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(3729866, 515471, 63269, '<td valign="top">Well, for the technical details it might have been nicer with maybe different lighting or more contrast or something... but otherwise this is beautiful. I love the model''s expression and pose. It looks like she was just sitting cross-legged and suddenly burst out screaming with laughter! The butterfly on her cheek adds the PERFECT touch, expecially with the selective desat. It matches her pose and gives the impression her soul is leaping with joy, if that makes any sense... :) Lovely capture.</td>', 'Well, for the technical details it might have been nicer with maybe different lighting or more contrast or something... but otherwise this is beautiful. I love the model''s expression and pose. It looks like she was just sitting cross-legged and suddenly burst out screaming with laughter! The butterfly on her cheek adds the PERFECT touch, expecially with the selective desat. It matches her pose and gives the impression her soul is leaping with joy, if that makes any sense... :) Lovely capture.', '2007-06-02 19:41:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(3729946, 515471, 51538, '<td valign="top">The outtake is nicely intimate.  I voted this a 6 but the outtake would have 7 from me.</td>', 'The outtake is nicely intimate.  I voted this a 6 but the outtake would have 7 from me.', '2007-06-02 20:24:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(3729949, 516826, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Wow what a fun shot! This is so creative! "Yikes" is a prefect entry into the Selective Desaturation challenge.  <br/> <br/>I was reading your comments and every one who stopped a looked loved this one, how could they not.  I think you did a great job with all the techs, the focus, lighting and overall composition are just excellent.  <br/> <br/>I think you are exactly right in saying that maybe with a fancier frame more people would have caught on to what you were capturing.  I wish I had more to say but you did an excellent job, I always love your work.<br/> <br/>Keep up the creative out of the box thinking! <br/></td>', '*Critique Club* Wow what a fun shot! This is so creative! "Yikes" is a prefect entry into the Selective Desaturation challenge.   I was reading your comments and every one who stopped a looked loved this one, how could they not.  I think you did a great job with all the techs, the focus, lighting and overall composition are just excellent.   I think you are exactly right in saying that maybe with a fancier frame more people would have caught on to what you were capturing.  I wish I had more to say but you did an excellent job, I always love your work. Keep up the creative out of the box thinking! ', '2007-06-02 20:26:32.000000', NULL, 0),
