(3733395, 514730, 73452, '<td valign="top">Philup, i think im in love with your hands.  haha, that sounds wierd.<br/>but anyways, i love this photo, the whole concept of it is beautiful!</td>', 'Philup, i think im in love with your hands.  haha, that sounds wierd.but anyways, i love this photo, the whole concept of it is beautiful!', '2007-06-03 19:32:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(3733731, 516030, 4226, '<td valign="top">** Critique club **<br/> <br/>Greetings from the critique club!<br/> <br/>I for one look at the title and the image both and see them together and this photograph goes very well with the title. Selective desaturation here works great with enhancing the subject and bringing it out.<br/> <br/>technically, you did a great job with masking for selective desaturation. I can see some noise in the image here. If possible I would shoot at lower ISO with a tripod since the subject is stationary. then you can allow for a higher dof at lower iso. I don''t know how the instrument actually looks, but the color tone varies a lot in the picture, could be possible with different light falling on the parts. I would try to control that with taking the pic in shade where the light is even, that should work well here IMO.<br/> <br/>Overall a good subject for selective desat. challenge. <br/> <br/>thanks,<br/>Gaurawa<br/></td>', '** Critique club ** Greetings from the critique club! I for one look at the title and the image both and see them together and this photograph goes very well with the title. Selective desaturation here works great with enhancing the subject and bringing it out. technically, you did a great job with masking for selective desaturation. I can see some noise in the image here. If possible I would shoot at lower ISO with a tripod since the subject is stationary. then you can allow for a higher dof at lower iso. I don''t know how the instrument actually looks, but the color tone varies a lot in the picture, could be possible with different light falling on the parts. I would try to control that with taking the pic in shade where the light is even, that should work well here IMO. Overall a good subject for selective desat. challenge.  thanks,Gaurawa', '2007-06-03 21:17:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(3733762, 513636, 71664, '<td valign="top">Hey I like this one, good job.  I gave it a 7 during voting.</td>', 'Hey I like this one, good job.  I gave it a 7 during voting.', '2007-06-03 21:28:30.000000', NULL, 0),
