(3976173, 516355, 7485, '<td valign="top">Hey, I just came across an identical pose in a photo by <a href="//www.dolgachov.com/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Lev Dolgachov</a>. It''s on the sixth page of his portfolio. So which one of you got the idea first? Either way, very well done!</td>', 'Hey, I just came across an identical pose in a photo by Lev Dolgachov. It''s on the sixth page of his portfolio. So which one of you got the idea first? Either way, very well done!', '2007-08-07 01:59:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(3982901, 516112, 69008, '<td valign="top">This is very nice, and has a good story to go with it. It makes me think about how it must have been to have lived at the time this was built, and to have done this kind of work. <br/>The image itself is well processed, with the grainy looking foreground, and selective desat to get the color to pop thru the window the way it does. The textures an lines where the stones fit to each other is a visual treat.</td>', 'This is very nice, and has a good story to go with it. It makes me think about how it must have been to have lived at the time this was built, and to have done this kind of work. The image itself is well processed, with the grainy looking foreground, and selective desat to get the color to pop thru the window the way it does. The textures an lines where the stones fit to each other is a visual treat.', '2007-08-09 01:51:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4001438, 516588, 77369, '<td valign="top">I would LOVE to know how you did this...I know how to manipulate eyes...s/c...etc...but how you get them to glow like this is amazing!!</td>', 'I would LOVE to know how you did this...I know how to manipulate eyes...s/c...etc...but how you get them to glow like this is amazing!!', '2007-08-15 15:30:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4001497, 516588, 63269, '<td valign="top">Thank you femalevsnature! It was pretty simple for the most part. I made two layers - one in color and one in black and white, with the black and white layer on top. I put the brush on "clear" and erased away eye from the black and white layer to revealt he colored iris underneath. The rest was some adjustments with the selective colors (specifically the cyan, blue, and the neutral levels,) and some contrast adjustments. For some added glow, I set the dodge to highlights and touch-up just the bottom of the iris. <br/> <br/>Hope this helps, and I''m glad you liked it!</td>', 'Thank you femalevsnature! It was pretty simple for the most part. I made two layers - one in color and one in black and white, with the black and white layer on top. I put the brush on "clear" and erased away eye from the black and white layer to revealt he colored iris underneath. The rest was some adjustments with the selective colors (specifically the cyan, blue, and the neutral levels,) and some contrast adjustments. For some added glow, I set the dodge to highlights and touch-up just the bottom of the iris.  Hope this helps, and I''m glad you liked it!', '2007-08-15 16:01:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4029088, 516885, 61651, '<td valign="top">I like this concept, and the selective saturation is done well, b&amp;w has good tones (great texture on that concrete).  Must be the petsitter in me. :)</td>', 'I like this concept, and the selective saturation is done well, b&w has good tones (great texture on that concrete).  Must be the petsitter in me. :)', '2007-08-25 23:46:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4043502, 516305, 47483, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by roz:</b></div><hr/><i> OMG ... i opened this and immediately loved it, so i scrolled down to see how it came in the challenge .. really, i am even more surprised about this one ... another RIDICULOUS score ... <br/>i dont think your title did you any favours tho, because i see this more like life, beauty, hope etc surrounded by broken dreams  ... they actually look like flowers on a grave, which would give this an even more dramatic feeling ... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Ditto.<br/> <br/>This does not deserve 4.9 by a long shot. It only proves that people have not taste for things. <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by roz: OMG ... i opened this and immediately loved it, so i scrolled down to see how it came in the challenge .. really, i am even more surprised about this one ... another RIDICULOUS score ... i dont think your title did you any favours tho, because i see this more like life, beauty, hope etc surrounded by broken dreams  ... they actually look like flowers on a grave, which would give this an even more dramatic feeling ...   Ditto. This does not deserve 4.9 by a long shot. It only proves that people have not taste for things. ', '2007-08-31 09:08:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4044813, 516685, 66597, '<td valign="top">I just noticed this in your profile, and I think it is amazing. In fact, I think you really got robbed on this. I love the lines and the contrast of the bright pink against the moody sky. Into faves. Bravo.</td>', 'I just noticed this in your profile, and I think it is amazing. In fact, I think you really got robbed on this. I love the lines and the contrast of the bright pink against the moody sky. Into faves. Bravo.', '2007-08-31 21:55:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(4064522, 516876, 53316, '<td valign="top">Love the contrast!!!</td>', 'Love the contrast!!!', '2007-09-06 08:25:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4081141, 513636, 40718, '<td valign="top">Technicals: lighting is nice.  I like the way the building facade pops out of the shadows.  The biggest technical issue, IMO, is the softness of the picture.  I don''t see what lens you used on the shot, but my first guess is it''s a product of the lens.  I see softness like this in the 75-300 a lot.<br/> <br/>The feel: I like the subjects you chose to selectively desat except the sign in the corner.  It pulls the eye away.  I know you couldn''t resist because it was such a nice red color, but perhaps doing a partial desat of it so it''s still red, but muted compared to the other colors.  My preference, however, would probably be to make it B&amp;W altogether.<br/> <br/>The game: Watch your border.  People, for some reason, don''t like a thick inner stripe.</td>', 'Technicals: lighting is nice.  I like the way the building facade pops out of the shadows.  The biggest technical issue, IMO, is the softness of the picture.  I don''t see what lens you used on the shot, but my first guess is it''s a product of the lens.  I see softness like this in the 75-300 a lot. The feel: I like the subjects you chose to selectively desat except the sign in the corner.  It pulls the eye away.  I know you couldn''t resist because it was such a nice red color, but perhaps doing a partial desat of it so it''s still red, but muted compared to the other colors.  My preference, however, would probably be to make it B&W altogether. The game: Watch your border.  People, for some reason, don''t like a thick inner stripe.', '2007-09-11 13:39:41.000000', NULL, 0),
